00:48:55.080 --> 00:48:56.080
of kind of an agape,

00:48:56.080 --> 00:48:59.080
a kind of sacrificial love.

00:48:59.080 --> 00:49:02.080
And when I think of this verse,

00:49:02.080 --> 00:49:03.080
you know, you could interpret it

00:49:03.080 --> 00:49:05.080
in a kind of dramatic fashion.

00:49:05.080 --> 00:49:06.080
You know, laying down

00:49:06.080 --> 00:49:07.080
your life for your friends,

00:49:07.080 --> 00:49:08.080
especially in light of,

00:49:08.080 --> 00:49:09.080
it's Christ who's saying it,

00:49:09.080 --> 00:49:10.080
so our minds immediately

00:49:10.080 --> 00:49:11.080
go to the cross,

00:49:11.080 --> 00:49:12.080
and it's sort of like the grand.

00:49:12.080 --> 00:49:13.080
And you could interpret it

00:49:13.080 --> 00:49:14.080
through a kind of grand gesture

00:49:14.080 --> 00:49:16.080
interpretation, you know,

00:49:16.080 --> 00:49:17.080
where it's sort of,

00:49:17.080 --> 00:49:19.080
yes, I'm willing to lay down my life.

00:49:19.080 --> 00:49:20.080
I would die for that person,

00:49:20.080 --> 00:49:22.080
that relationship.

00:49:22.080 --> 00:49:24.080
And that has its place, I agree.

00:49:24.080 --> 00:49:26.080
That's a beautiful act of love.

00:49:26.080 --> 00:49:29.080
But I want to interpret it

00:49:29.080 --> 00:49:30.080
more through that,

00:49:30.080 --> 00:49:32.080
the dailiness of living.

00:49:32.080 --> 00:49:33.080
You know, isn't there something

00:49:33.080 --> 00:49:35.080
about just showing up

00:49:35.080 --> 00:49:38.080
for the people, the friends,

00:49:38.080 --> 00:49:40.080
the community, the family

00:49:40.080 --> 00:49:42.080
that we love?

00:49:42.080 --> 00:49:44.080
And like, it's those little acts

00:49:44.080 --> 00:49:46.080
of kindness, those little deaths,

00:49:46.080 --> 00:49:48.080
those giving of ourselves

00:49:48.080 --> 00:49:49.080
in that way.

00:49:49.080 --> 00:49:51.080
Like, this is the very foundation

00:49:51.080 --> 00:49:55.080
of love and relationship.

00:49:55.080 --> 00:49:57.080
And it's important to name,

00:49:57.080 --> 00:49:58.080
it's not that saying,

00:49:58.080 --> 00:49:59.080
I don't matter,

00:49:59.080 --> 00:50:01.080
or my needs don't matter.

00:50:01.080 --> 00:50:02.080
Of course, this can,

00:50:02.080 --> 00:50:04.080
agape can take its own,

00:50:04.080 --> 00:50:06.080
sort of get weird and abusive,

00:50:06.080 --> 00:50:07.080
and you know,

00:50:07.080 --> 00:50:09.080
so I'm not saying do that.

00:50:09.080 --> 00:50:12.080
But on the other hand,

00:50:12.080 --> 00:50:13.080
we'd be kidding ourselves

00:50:13.080 --> 00:50:14.080
if we didn't say,

00:50:14.080 --> 00:50:16.080
there is something sacrificial,

00:50:16.080 --> 00:50:19.080
you know, about love

00:50:19.080 --> 00:50:20.080
and really what it means,

00:50:20.080 --> 00:50:23.080
what it looks like.

00:50:23.080 --> 00:50:24.080
If you've ever read

00:50:24.080 --> 00:50:25.080
the pastoral letters

00:50:25.080 --> 00:50:26.080
in the New Testament,

00:50:26.080 --> 00:50:27.080
books like, you know,

00:50:27.080 --> 00:50:28.080
Romans and Colossians

00:50:28.080 --> 00:50:29.080
and Ephesians and all that,

00:50:29.080 --> 00:50:31.080
they often end

00:50:31.080 --> 00:50:33.080
with something like this.

00:50:33.080 --> 00:50:34.080
This one's from Colossians,

00:50:34.080 --> 00:50:35.080
from chapter four,

00:50:35.080 --> 00:50:36.080
verses 10 through 15.

00:50:36.080 --> 00:50:37.080
Paul writes,

00:50:37.080 --> 00:50:39.080
My fellow prisoner Aristarchus

00:50:39.080 --> 00:50:40.080
sends you his greetings,

00:50:40.080 --> 00:50:41.080
as does Mark,

00:50:41.080 --> 00:50:43.080
the cousin of Barnabas.

00:50:43.080 --> 00:50:44.080
You've received instructions

00:50:44.080 --> 00:50:45.080
about him.

00:50:45.080 --> 00:50:46.080
If he comes to you,

00:50:46.080 --> 00:50:47.080
welcome him.

00:50:47.080 --> 00:50:49.080
Jesus, who is called Justice,

00:50:49.080 --> 00:50:50.080
I guess they kind of

00:50:50.080 --> 00:50:51.080
changed his name

00:50:51.080 --> 00:50:52.080
because it was a little awkward

00:50:52.080 --> 00:50:53.080
to keep calling him Jesus,

00:50:53.080 --> 00:50:54.080
who is called Justice,

00:50:54.080 --> 00:50:55.080
he also sends greetings.

00:50:55.080 --> 00:50:56.080
These are the only Jews

00:50:56.080 --> 00:50:57.080
among my co-workers

00:50:57.080 --> 00:50:58.080
for the kingdom of God,

00:50:58.080 --> 00:50:59.080
and they've proved

00:50:59.080 --> 00:51:00.080
a comfort to me.

00:51:00.080 --> 00:51:02.080
Epaphras, who is one of you

00:51:02.080 --> 00:51:03.080
and a servant of Christ Jesus,

00:51:03.080 --> 00:51:04.080
sends greetings.

00:51:04.080 --> 00:51:06.080
He's always wrestling

00:51:06.080 --> 00:51:07.080
in prayer for you,

00:51:07.080 --> 00:51:08.080
that you may stand firm

00:51:08.080 --> 00:51:09.080
in the will of God,

00:51:09.080 --> 00:51:11.080
mature and fully assured.

00:51:11.080 --> 00:51:12.080
I vouch for him

00:51:12.080 --> 00:51:13.080
that he's working hard for you,

00:51:13.080 --> 00:51:15.080
and for those at Laodicea

00:51:15.080 --> 00:51:16.080
and Hierapolis.

00:51:16.080 --> 00:51:17.080
Our dear friend Luke,

00:51:17.080 --> 00:51:18.080
the doctor,

00:51:18.080 --> 00:51:19.080
who wrote famously

00:51:19.080 --> 00:51:20.080
the Gospel of Luke,

00:51:20.080 --> 00:51:21.080
and Demas,

00:51:21.080 --> 00:51:22.080
send greetings

00:51:22.080 --> 00:51:23.080
and give my greetings

00:51:23.080 --> 00:51:24.080
to the brothers and sisters

00:51:24.080 --> 00:51:26.080
at Laodicea and to Nympha

00:51:26.080 --> 00:51:30.080
and the church in her house.

00:51:30.080 --> 00:51:31.080
What's the takeaway there?

00:51:31.080 --> 00:51:33.080
Can you see that even

00:51:33.080 --> 00:51:35.080
in its very earliest days,

00:51:35.080 --> 00:51:38.080
like the church has never been

00:51:39.080 --> 00:51:42.080
about celebrity pastors

00:51:42.080 --> 00:51:46.080
or solo spiritual entrepreneurs.

00:51:46.080 --> 00:51:47.080
Like, no, no, no.

00:51:47.080 --> 00:51:50.080
The church is always rooted in,

00:51:50.080 --> 00:51:51.080
yes, first the love of God

00:51:51.080 --> 00:51:52.080
and Christ,

00:51:52.080 --> 00:51:55.080
but then as that finds,

00:51:55.080 --> 00:51:56.080
kind of it's planted

00:51:56.080 --> 00:51:59.080
in like the soil of community.

00:51:59.080 --> 00:52:01.080
It's a communal love.

00:52:01.080 --> 00:52:04.080
It is about the people here

00:52:04.080 --> 00:52:06.080
learning to love one another

00:52:06.080 --> 00:52:09.080
in real and powerful ways.

00:52:09.080 --> 00:52:11.080
But what I'm driving at, though,

00:52:11.080 --> 00:52:12.080
is we are living in a culture

00:52:12.080 --> 00:52:15.080
that is kind of pushing back on this.

00:52:15.080 --> 00:52:16.080
That's sort of,

00:52:16.080 --> 00:52:17.080
it's not like an active push.

00:52:17.080 --> 00:52:19.080
It's more of a kind of passive,

00:52:19.080 --> 00:52:20.080
like eroding,

00:52:20.080 --> 00:52:22.080
you know, like the way maybe

00:52:22.080 --> 00:52:25.080
a river kind of erodes the bank

00:52:25.080 --> 00:52:28.080
of, you know, kind of its side.

00:52:28.080 --> 00:52:29.080
It's just kind of over time,

00:52:29.080 --> 00:52:30.080
and that's kind of how I see

00:52:30.080 --> 00:52:31.080
secular culture.

00:52:31.080 --> 00:52:32.080
It's just kind of eroding

00:52:32.080 --> 00:52:33.080
relationships,

00:52:33.080 --> 00:52:35.080
eroding social connections

00:52:36.080 --> 00:52:38.080
and ultimately even at times

00:52:38.080 --> 00:52:40.080
really impacting churches.

00:52:40.080 --> 00:52:42.080
And I think it's really time

00:52:42.080 --> 00:52:45.080
for us to, as best we can,

00:52:45.080 --> 00:52:47.080
start to kind of push back on this.

00:52:47.080 --> 00:52:51.080
To really start to invest,

00:52:51.080 --> 00:52:54.080
not just in like simulated

00:52:54.080 --> 00:52:57.080
online virtual living,

00:52:57.080 --> 00:52:59.080
but like coming back,

00:52:59.080 --> 00:53:02.080
coming back to flesh and blood

00:53:02.080 --> 00:53:04.080
relationships.

00:53:04.080 --> 00:53:06.080
Like people,

00:53:06.080 --> 00:53:09.080
people that matter to us.

00:53:09.080 --> 00:53:10.080
And then learning

00:53:10.080 --> 00:53:12.080
to engage agape love

00:53:12.080 --> 00:53:14.080
even then and there.

00:53:14.080 --> 00:53:18.080
So let's start to kind of push back.

00:53:18.080 --> 00:53:20.080
You know, let's begin

00:53:20.080 --> 00:53:22.080
to rediscover how God

00:53:22.080 --> 00:53:24.080
made us to be.

00:53:24.080 --> 00:53:26.080
Let's be open to sacrificing

00:53:26.080 --> 00:53:27.080
for one another

00:53:27.080 --> 00:53:28.080
and allowing others

00:53:28.080 --> 00:53:30.080
to sacrifice for us.

00:53:30.080 --> 00:53:32.080
And of course here at the table

00:53:32.080 --> 00:53:33.080
a lot of how we do this

00:53:33.080 --> 00:53:35.080
is through our meetups.

00:53:35.080 --> 00:53:36.080
If you're not part of one,

00:53:36.080 --> 00:53:38.080
I encourage you to go online

00:53:38.080 --> 00:53:40.080
or later we'll have the QR code

00:53:40.080 --> 00:53:41.080
that has the link tree

00:53:41.080 --> 00:53:44.080
that you can go find one there.

00:53:44.080 --> 00:53:45.080
But those are beautiful

00:53:45.080 --> 00:53:46.080
little expressions,

00:53:46.080 --> 00:53:48.080
like little outposts of people.

00:53:48.080 --> 00:53:49.080
Yeah, we're fumbling

00:53:49.080 --> 00:53:50.080
and bumbling around.

00:53:50.080 --> 00:53:51.080
I'm not trying to say like

00:53:51.080 --> 00:53:53.080
these are perfect communities really.

00:53:53.080 --> 00:53:54.080
No, no.

00:53:54.080 --> 00:53:56.080
These are real people.

00:53:56.080 --> 00:53:58.080
But there is something beautiful

00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:00.080
as folks learn to relate

00:54:00.080 --> 00:54:02.080
and sacrifice

00:54:02.080 --> 00:54:04.080
and show up for one another.

00:54:04.080 --> 00:54:07.080
So let's have these values

00:54:07.080 --> 00:54:08.080
for us, you know,

00:54:08.080 --> 00:54:10.080
communal, vulnerable.

00:54:10.080 --> 00:54:11.080
Let's have these,

00:54:11.080 --> 00:54:12.080
not just be like bullet points

00:54:12.080 --> 00:54:14.080
on the website,

00:54:14.080 --> 00:54:15.080
but something where

00:54:15.080 --> 00:54:17.080
we're really living

00:54:17.080 --> 00:54:18.080
as we press in

00:54:18.080 --> 00:54:19.080
to the love of God

00:54:19.080 --> 00:54:20.080
and what community

00:54:20.080 --> 00:54:21.080
actually can mean

00:54:21.080 --> 00:54:24.080
here in the 21st century.

00:54:24.080 --> 00:54:25.080
So in the name of the Father,

00:54:25.080 --> 00:54:27.080
the Son, and the Holy Spirit.

00:54:27.080 --> 00:54:28.080
Amen.

00:54:29.080 --> 00:54:32.080
So on the night

00:54:32.080 --> 00:54:34.080
that Jesus was betrayed,

00:54:34.080 --> 00:54:35.080
he had one final meal

00:54:35.080 --> 00:54:37.080
with his disciples.

00:54:37.080 --> 00:54:38.080
And at that meal,

00:54:38.080 --> 00:54:39.080
he held up a loaf of bread

00:54:39.080 --> 00:54:40.080
and he broke it

00:54:40.080 --> 00:54:41.080
and he said,

00:54:41.080 --> 00:54:42.080
take it and eat.

00:54:42.080 --> 00:54:43.080
This is my body.

00:54:43.080 --> 00:54:44.080
It's broken for you.

00:54:44.080 --> 00:54:46.080
And he held up a cup of wine.

00:54:46.080 --> 00:54:47.080
He said, take it and drink.

00:54:47.080 --> 00:54:48.080
This is my blood.

00:54:48.080 --> 00:54:50.080
It's shed for you.

00:54:50.080 --> 00:54:51.080
Whenever you eat this bread,

00:54:51.080 --> 00:54:53.080
whenever you drink this cup,

00:54:53.080 --> 00:54:55.080
remember me.

00:54:55.080 --> 00:54:57.080
So as we come forward today,

00:54:57.080 --> 00:54:58.080
may it be a kind of

00:54:58.080 --> 00:54:59.080
moment of solidarity,

00:54:59.080 --> 00:55:00.080
may it be a moment

00:55:00.080 --> 00:55:01.080
of community

00:55:01.080 --> 00:55:02.080
as we partake

00:55:02.080 --> 00:55:04.080
of the one body of Christ

00:55:04.080 --> 00:55:06.080
and find ourselves

00:55:06.080 --> 00:55:07.080
kind of enveloped

00:55:07.080 --> 00:55:08.080
in his body.

00:55:08.080 --> 00:55:09.080
And through that,

00:55:09.080 --> 00:55:10.080
there's a sense of connectedness

00:55:10.080 --> 00:55:11.080
and communion.

00:55:11.080 --> 00:55:12.080
That's why it's called communion,

00:55:12.080 --> 00:55:13.080
right?

00:55:13.080 --> 00:55:15.080
Connection through that.

00:55:15.080 --> 00:55:16.080
So we'll just go

00:55:16.080 --> 00:55:17.080
row by row here,

00:55:17.080 --> 00:55:18.080
starting at the front.

00:55:18.080 --> 00:55:19.080
We'll form one line.

